<title>UK: HILLSDOWN UP ON NATWEST UPGRADE.</title>
<headline>HILLSDOWN UP ON NATWEST UPGRADE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Hillsdown Holdings Plc resumed their recovery on Tuesday after NatWest upgraded its rating on the stock to &quot;add&quot; from &quot;hold,&quot; dealers said.</p>
<p>At 0925 GMT, the shares were up 5-1/2p to 169.  </p>
<p>The analyst wasn't immediately available to comment, but market sources said the upgrade was part of a general re-weighting within the sector, with a bias toward second-line food manufacturers.</p>
<p>NatWest also reduced its recommendation on Cadbury Schweppes Plc to &quot;reduce&quot; from &quot;hold,&quot; market sources said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
